.TH std::layout_left_padded 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::layout_left_padded \- std::layout_left_padded

.SH Synopsis
Defined in header <mdspan>
template< std::size_t PaddingValue = std::dynamic_extent >  (since C++26)
struct layout_left_padded;

Every specialization of layout_left_padded is a LayoutMappingPolicy which provides a
layout mapping that is similar to layout_left::mapping except that it has a padding
stride.

Every specialization of layout_left_padded is TriviallyCopyable, and
std::is_trivially_default_constructible_v<T> is true for any such specialization T.

Let m be the instance of the mapping type layout_left_padded::mapping. The padding stride
of the mapping is the second stride m.stride\fB(1)\fP which is guaranteed to be at least the
first extent value m.extent\fB(0)\fP, called extent to pad.

  Nested class templates

mapping a layout mapping of layout_left_padded
        \fI(public member class template)\fP

